==English==

===Etymology===
Probably from {{etyl|dum|en}} {{term|clompe|lang=dum}} or {{etyl|gml|en}} {{term|klumpe|lang=gml}}<ref>[http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/clump%5B1%5D clump] in Merriam-Webster's dictionary</ref> (compare German {{term|Klumpen}}). Cognates include Danish {{term|klump|lang=da}} (probably from Low German as well<ref>{{R:ODS online|klump}}</ref>). Compare Norwegian (bokmål) {{term|klump|lang=no}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-clump.ogg|Audio (US)}}
*: {{rhymes|ʌmp}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[cluster]] or [[lump]]
# A [[thick]] [[group]] or [[bunch]], especially of [[bush]]es or hair.
# A [[dull]] [[thud]].

====Derived terms====
* [[clumpy]]

